jobs.description:
• Conduct in-depth analyses of P&L, ROCE, and risk management for specific market segments, identifying trends and growth potential;
• Translate financial data into clear reports and presentations, providing strategic insights and recommendations;
• Optimize working capital and monitor key risks related to accumulated positions and essential raw materials;
• Manage the planning process, including periodic forecasts, annual budgeting, and strategic planning up to EBIT level;
• Contribute to key investment projects, including CAPEX and M&A, by providing financial expertise;
• Collaborate with the Reporting Factory to enhance reporting and analysis tools, ensuring consistency and accuracy;
• Act as a strong business partner by supporting market segments and facilitating strategic decisions with financial insights.

Must-haves:

• You hold a master’s degree in finance, business administration, or a related field;
• Acquire at least 4 years of experience in finance, preferably as a controller or business partner;
• Demonstrate strong analytical skills to translate financial data into strategic insights;
• Communicate fluently in Dutch, both written and spoken;
• Possess excellent communication skills to present complex financial concepts clearly;
• Collaborate effectively with cross-functional teams and senior management.
Nice-to-haves:

• Have experience working with SAP or similar ERP systems.
• Speak English or French in addition to Dutch.
• Show a proactive mindset with a hands-on approach to problem-solving.
• Bring experience in investment analysis, CAPEX, or M&A.
